<title>NETHERLANDS: Lucent wins $12 million Swedish telecom deal.</title>
<headline>Lucent wins $12 million Swedish telecom deal.</headline>
<dateline>HILVERSUM, Netherlands 1996-09-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Telecoms equipment maker Lucent Technologies said on Monday it had won a $12 million contract from Swedish telecom giant Telia AB to expand its voice and data transmission network.</p>
<p>&quot;Under the agreement Lucent Technologies will supply its ATM (Asynchronous Transfer Mode) equipment...(and) maintenance support to Telia,&quot; the company said in a statement.</p>
<p>The equipment will enable state-owned Telia to manage its entire ATM network from a central location, Lucent said.</p>
<p>Lucent, the former equipment arm of AT&amp;T Corp, has based its European headquarters in Hilversum.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
